contentText:
Drake turned a handful of tracks premiered during his FOMO short film into a four-pack of songs that landed on streaming services on Friday (Oct. 2).

The 6 God initially teased that a &#8220;bunch of songs&#8221; would be coming to DSPs earlier this week while streaming a gambling session on Kick.

“Go watch&nbsp; FOMO . It’s a bunch of songs coming to streaming on Thursday,” Drake said. “So, all the songs that you guys have been asking [about]. Well, not all of them. Enough of them are coming on Thursday. That’s it.&#8221;

The foursome includes a pair of Don Toliver collaborations, including &#8220;Solar Eclipse,&#8221; which is best known for Drake&#8217;s interpolation of Ella Langley&#8217;s &#8220;Choosin&#8217; Texas&#8221; anthem that&#8217;s spending a record 24th week atop the Billboard Hot 100.

Fans also got their wish as the dynamic &#8220;Cold Shoulder&#8221; featuring Toliver was brought to DSPs, along with an extended version of HABIBT I&#8217;s &#8220;Classic&#8221; and &#8220;Quebec.&#8221;

Drake&#8217;s four-pack arrives a week after Taylor Swift employed a similar strategy with her foursome of new tracks packaged as The Life of a Showgirl: The Encore .

It remains to be seen if the hype and appetite for Drizzy&#8217;s fresh tunes is as fervent as a few weeks ago when it comes to his future charting success, since all four songs were debuted on Sept. 15 in Fear of Missing Out .

Either way, Drake fans are eating well in 2026 and the 6 God&#8217;s creative juices are flowing effortlessly. Back in May, Drizzy picked up a 15th No. 1 album atop the Billboard 200 with ICEMAN and he notched a 14th No. 1 smash on the Billboard Hot 100 thanks to &#8220;Janice STFU.&#8221;

Drake&#8217;s May trifecta (ICEMAN , HABIBTI and MAID OF HONOUR ) also made history with the OVO boss becoming the first artist to ever hold the top three slots on the Billboard 200 simultaneously.

